  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Widespread soaking rain expected Thursday. Some\ndrought relief is possible, but flooding is not expected.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nConfidence is increasing in a widespread soaking rain for \nThursday. The setup involves an upper level trough approaching \nfrom the northwest and amplifying over the region, with surface \nlow pressure likely developing just offshore Thursday. Guidance\nhas slowed the system down slightly with rain now not expected\nuntil Wednesday night with a steady, widespread stratiform rain\nThursday. A 30 to 50% chance of rainfall exceeding 1 inch exists\nthrough the end of the day on Thursday with the highest\nprobabilities further south associated with strengthening low\npressure just offshore. Some fog is also possible Wednesday\nnight as weak southerly flow brings moisture onshore.\n\nGuidance continues to emphasize the possibility of rainy conditions\npersisting into Friday and possibly early Saturday as low \npressure dives southeast through the area. Rain will likely be \nin the form of showers rather than the steady rain on Thursday.",
